            "inlineStyleRanges": [],
            "key": "659ng",
            "text": "Qwen3.8-27B-4-bit-on-a-single-DGX-Spark",
            "type": "unstyled"
          },
          {
            "data": {},
            "entityRanges": [],
            "inlineStyleRanges": [],
            "key": "900nb",
            "text": "Two 4-bit checkpoints measured against the FP8 baseline on the same harness, so the quantization gain is isolated.",
            "type": "unstyled"
          },
          {
            "data": {},
            "entityRanges": [],
            "inlineStyleRanges": [
              {
                "length": 22,
                "offset": 0,
                "style": "Bold"
              }
            ],
            "key": "ehku1",
            "text": "Checkpoint comparison: NVFP4 vs MixedInt4-AutoRound on decode, concurrency, prefill and KV capacity. They tie on single-stream decode and nowhere else",
            "type": "unordered-list-item"
          },
          {
            "data": {},
            "entityRanges": [],
            "inlineStyleRanges": [
              {
                "length": 15,
                "offset": 0,
                "style": "Bold"
              },
              {
                "length": 25,
                "offset": 121,
                "style": "Italic"
              }
            ],
            "key": "dnh44",
            "text": "SM121 guidance: why W4A16 beats W4A4 on hardware with no native FP4 path, and the one environment variable that prevents silently incorrect output",
            "type": "unordered-list-item"
          },
          {
            "data": {},
            "entityRanges": [],
            "inlineStyleRanges": [
              {
                "length": 18,
                "offset": 0,
                "style": "Bold"
              }
            ],
            "key": "1gcja",
            "text": "Layer sensitivity: which projections must stay in higher precision on this hybrid architecture, and why a generic \"quantize every Linear\" recipe damages it",
            "type": "unordered-list-item"
          },
          {
            "data": {},
            "entityRanges": [],
            "inlineStyleRanges": [
              {
                "length": 15,
                "offset": 0,
                "style": "Bold"
              }
            ],
            "key": "7p485",
            "text": "LIMITATIONS.md: both repos carry one, stating plainly what was not measured, where sample sizes are thin, and which earlier conclusions the later data overturned",
            "type": "unordered-list-item"
          },
          {
            "data": {},
            "entityRanges": [],
            "inlineStyleRanges": [
              {
                "length": 8,
                "offset": 35,
                "style": "Bold"
              }
            ],
            "key": "3cpnn",
            "text": "If you only read one file, make it NOTES.md in the FP8 repo. Most of what is in there is not in any documentation, it came from reading engine source to work out why a default was not what it appeared to be.",
            "type": "unstyled"
          }
        ],
